OL,3,GNEWSA'Extremist' jailed for raping     
OL,4,Awoman in her home                      
OL,6,FAn alleged terrorist has been jailed   
OL,7,Ffor six years for raping a woman whose 
OL,8,Fmobile phone recording provided key    
OL,9,Fevidence in the trial.                 
OL,11,FAyman Al-Shammari, 28, a refugee from  
OL,12,FKuwait living in Taunton, Somerset, was
OL,13,Fsentenced to six years on Friday at    
OL,14,FBristol Crown Court after being found  
OL,15,Fguilty of rape in October.             
OL,17,FThe jury heard that Al-Shammari had    
OL,18,Fconsensual sex with a woman in her 20s,
OL,19,Fbut when she told him to stop, he      
OL,20,Fcontinued. Austria has now requested   
OL,21,Fthe extradition of Al-Shammari on      
OL,22,Fterrorism charges.                     
OL,23,APub: 27-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
